            "title": "Grainger (GWW): Net Margin Slides to 9.7%, Testing Premium Valuation Narrative",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "W.W. Grainger (GWW) has posted 19% annual earnings growth over the last five years. Over the past year, however, earnings growth turned negative and net profit margins dipped from 10.8% to 9.7%. Looking ahead, earnings are projected to grow at 10.37% per year, while revenue is forecast to rise by 6.1% annually. This revenue growth outlook trails the broader U.S. market\u2019s projected 10.4% revenue growth. Despite the company\u2019s consistent earnings quality, its shares trade at a premium...",
